WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.532
I need the Department of Higher Education.

00:00:02.692 --> 00:00:03.609
Tab to About.

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:04.498
Down arrow.

00:00:04.658 --> 00:00:05.737
Where did the link go?

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.458
I turn on Curb Cut.

00:00:08.618 --> 00:00:09.429
Same menu.

00:00:09.589 --> 00:00:10.552
Same keyboard.

00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:11.409
There it is.

00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:12.435
The DHE.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.319
Kane tries the same task with a mouse.

00:00:17.479 --> 00:00:19.086
The department page opens.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.716
With keys alone, Kane cannot reach that link.

00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:25.833
Now we have a reproducible failure.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.132
Here’s a failure that went straight back to the coding agent.

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:32.047
Watch the converter’s answer field.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.404
At this width, the field runs off the screen.

00:00:35.564 --> 00:00:39.975
Codex receives Kane’s failed assertion and writes a rule to stack the cells.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.322
Kane runs it again.

00:00:43.482 --> 00:00:44.217
One meter.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.590
The answer is visible.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.284
At Munich Airport, listen to the previous slide control.

00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:50.890
[Reading voice] Button.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.234
[Reading voice] Vorherige Folie.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.559
On Meridiano, two buttons have no names.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:59.068
TypeSafe Jev names them in about a second.

00:00:59.228 --> 00:00:59.584
[Reading voice] Menú.

00:00:59.744 --> 00:01:00.274
[Reading voice] Buscar.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.681
The site owner gets the task, the recordings, and a source repair.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.110
One hundred five fixes are live.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.632
Get Curb Cut for Chrome.
